{
  "case_id": "2008-08-205",
  "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Participation in the political process is the First Amendment's most fundamental guarantee. Yet that freedom is being smothered by one of the most complicated, expensive, and incomprehensible regulatory regimes ever invented by the administrative state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Olson, if the film were distributed by General Motors, would your argument be the same?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Was that -- was that established? I thought that the record was hardly made of the contributors to this film."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You say that. Why -- what -- what is your basis for saying that Congress is -- is less concerned with 90 minutes of don't vote for Clinton than it was with 60 seconds of don't vote?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because -- because the record in Congress and the record in this Court is that those types of advertisements were more effective because they came into your home --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stewart",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The lead opinion in Wisconsin Right to Life didn't just use the term \"functional equivalent of express advocacy\"; it explained what that term meant, and on page 2667 of volume 127 of the Supreme Court Reporter, the plurality or the lead opinion stated: \"In light of these considerations, a Court should find that an ad is the functional equivalent of express advocacy only if the ad is susceptible of no reasonable interpretation other than as an appeal to vote for or against a specific candidate.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But does \"the press\" mean the media in that Constitutional provision? You think in 1791 there were -- there were people running around with fedoras that had press -- little press tickets in it, \"Press\"? Is that what \"press\" means in the Constitution? Doesn't it cover the Xerox machine? Doesn't it cover the right of any individual to -- to write, to publish?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If they had done either of the things you just mentioned, putting it on its Web site or putting it on YouTube, your position would be that the Constitution would permit the prohibition of that during the period prior to the primary or the election?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Citizens United)",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is not that the Constitution would permit it. Our position is that BCRA wouldn't prohibit it because those are not covered media."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: This film has been compared to \"Fahrenheit 911,\" which had the pervasive message that President Bush was unsuited to be President. And so if that film had been financed out of corporate -- corporations' general treasury funds and put on an election channel, that would similarly be banned by the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Stewart, do you think that there's a possibility that the First Amendment interest is greater when what the government is trying to stifle is not just a speaker who wants to say something but also a hearer who wants to hear what the speaker has to say?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, before you run out here, can I -- we haven't talked about the disclosure requirements yet. You understand the test to be that disclosure is not required if the names of those disclosed -- if those people would be reasonably subject to reprisals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Olson, can I ask this question? Coming up with Wisconsin Right to Life, Judge Randolph thought the Chief Justice's opinion in that case was controlling in that case. Do you think the Chief Justice's opinion in that case correctly stated the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel.\nThe case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:11 a.m., the case in the\nabove-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "bc49fcc528e1f486e8641ed75817185c5a5c966e772056fb45b3c6aa0d7dcd3c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc49fcc528e1-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The other thing is I heard Justice -- I mean\nMr. Stewart say that there's one minute at the\nbeginning, it doesn't happen -- it doesn't matter what\nthe other 89 minutes are; we can prohibit it."
    },
    {
